From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:15:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Drop the 20/40 MHz scan callback of a disabled link

For EVENT_SCAN_RESULTS, wpa_supplicant_event() calls the scan callback
of each partner link that has one. hostapd_stop_setup_timers() cancels
the retry of the 20/40 MHz coexistence scan, but keeps iface->scan_cb,
so a link disabled during that scan keeps ieee80211n_check_scan(). When
the results arrive, the partner loop runs it on the disabled link, whose
drv_priv is NULL, and hostapd crashes in
wpa_driver_nl80211_get_scan_results(). Reachable with DISABLE of an AP
MLD link in HAPD_IFACE_HT_SCAN.

Drop the callback when the setup timers stop.

Fixes: 9b682e72d9d1 ("AP MLD: Find the link that is waiting for scan events")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/hw_features.c
+++ b/src/ap/hw_features.c
@@ -612,6 +612,10 @@ static void ap_ht40_scan_retry(void *elo
 void hostapd_stop_setup_timers(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 {
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(ap_ht40_scan_retry, iface, NULL);
+
+	/* The scan results can still arrive through a partner link */
+	if (iface->scan_cb == ieee80211n_check_scan)
+		iface->scan_cb = NULL;
 }
 
 
